BT /F1 14 Tf 72 720 Td 14 TL (Cell Structure and Function The mitochondrion is known as the powerhouse of the cell. It produces ATP through oxidative phosphorylation. The nucleus contains the cell's genetic material and coordinates activities such as growth and metabolism. Ribosomes synthesize proteins by translating messenger RNA into polypeptide chains. The cell membrane is a selectively permeable barrier composed of a phospholipid bilayer. Photosynthesis occurs in chloroplasts, converting light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. Study tip: compare and contrast mitochondria and chloroplasts for your next quiz.) Tj ET
